 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The veterinarian directory answers which specialties a veterinarian holds; staff also ask the inverse. The clinic publishes every specialty it knows by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-VET-003]`. Each veterinarian appears by full name, first name then last name. All specialties appear on one page, without paging. The page lists specialties, not the full roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears under none. The view is read-only, and the page is reached by its address alone: no navigation entry or link from another page leads to it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name on a single page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty held by veterinarians, when the specialty directory is opened, then each holder is listed under it by first name then last name, for example "Helen Leary".
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears under no specialty.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the specialty directory is opened, then the specialty is listed and shown as having no veterinarians.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given any other page of the system, when it is rendered, then it carries no navigation entry or link to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A veterinarian holding several specialties appears under each one.
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+3. The page's wording is present in every supported language, as `REQ-LANG-002` requires.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
